From: tas0dev <156896971+tas0dev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 09:40:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] x86/mboot: arm GPU watchdog before readiness

Hardware Domain readiness now depends on the userspace GPU renderer owning its
control endpoint.  The renderer watchdog was still armed only after that same
readiness transition, so it could never report a renderer which failed to
start.  Schedule it while readiness is waiting and do not postpone an already
pending timeout on every retry.
---
 arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mboot.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mboot.c b/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mboot.c
index 333333333333..444444444444 100644
--- a/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mboot.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mboot.c
@@ -3752,6 +3752,10 @@ static void mboot_ready_workfn(struct work_struct *work)
 {
 	mboot_reprobe_display();
 	if (!mboot_display_backend_ready()) {
+		/* Do not reset the deadline on each 100 ms readiness retry. */
+		if (!READ_ONCE(mboot_gpu_open))
+			schedule_delayed_work(&mboot_gpu_watchdog_work,
+					      msecs_to_jiffies(5000));
 		/* The DRM framebuffer can appear before the userspace renderer has
 		 * completed EGL setup and its first KMS commit. */
 		mod_delayed_work(system_wq, &mboot_ready_work,
@@ -3765,8 +3769,6 @@ static void mboot_ready_workfn(struct work_struct *work)
 		pr_err("mDriver: hardware backend startup failed\n");
 		return;
 	}
-	mod_delayed_work(system_wq, &mboot_gpu_watchdog_work,
-			 msecs_to_jiffies(10000));
 }
 
 static int mboot_fb_event(struct notifier_block *notifier,
